s they come  forward the crush is there as  connect well is gonna get taken down and  now faker's in for the cleanup the  rockets will land and i have no idea in  hell how t1 did that also the meta kind  of suits faker right now he's been able  to play a lot of leblanc this split and  we all know just how disgusting he is on  that champ but we've also got to see him  on other old faithfuls such as azir and  a reworked arri now i used to watch  faker play arry  years ago i used to learn lows from him  i don't want to say how many years ago  that was but the point is he hasn't lost  it while faker looks to keep this insane  win streak going he's also been knocking  down some personal milestones too in  early march he hit two and a half  thousand career kills in the lck over  twice as much as some other people on  the top 15 leaderboard and this came  less than a month after he celebrated an  astounding 1 000 games in the lck being  only second to this record to deft who  incredibly actually achieved it the day  before faker the point is things seem to  be coming together for faker at the  moment he's dominating these  leaderboards of the all-time korean  greats but the difference between him  and a lot of them is he's still going  faker has always had natural skill but  the past few years have also shown what  a stable leader he can be for the young  talent that surrounds him he's been to  the mountaintop quite a few times  actually nobody has seen more success  than him in league of legends any young  player that plays with him is naturally  going to absorb some of that experience  and mentality after world's last year  faker committed to t1 for the entirety  of 2022 so we know he's going to be with  them and continue playing for at least  this year but what happens after that  any conversation about faker's longevity  always includes speculation about when  this superhuman is finally gonna pack it  in and retire let me tell you there  aren't many pros from 2013 still  knocking about now romantics will always  say faker will never retire until he  wins worlds one final time now a year or  two ago i would have laughed at that but  now  maybe not worlds this year will mark six  years since faker last lifted its trophy  it's been six years of shifting metas  new korean dynasties the domination of  china and europe showing up at times not  to mention minor regions drawing some  serious blood sure you could never  really write faker off during this time  but now especially with this record  being broken things feel a bit different  ltk playoffs are right around the corner  and i highly encourage you to join me in  watching them because i truly think we  might be witnessing the return of the  king here i don't want to get too  carried away here obviously i know it's  only march but  but if faker does win worlds this year  and then he retires you're going to want  to say you were here for it  okay  oh that kind of hurt my eyes

